-- Q3780: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["ISO 27001 information security management standard","NIST Cybersecurity Framework for risk management","COSO Internal Control — Integrated Framework (2013)","COBIT 2019 governance and management framework"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the AICPA Trust Services Criteria (TSC 2017), the common criteria CC1 through CC9 are deliberately mapped to the 17 principles of the COSO Internal Control—Integrated Framework (2013). CC1 maps to control environment, CC2 to communication, and CC3 to risk assessment.
Wrong (A): ISO 27001 is an information security standard but is not the framework upon which the common criteria are structurally based.
Wrong (B): The NIST Cybersecurity Framework addresses cybersecurity risk management but does not serve as the structural foundation for TSC common criteria.
Wrong (D): COBIT 2019 is an IT governance framework but the TSC common criteria are aligned to COSO, not COBIT.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3780;

-- Q3781: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["How the entity communicates internally about control responsibilities","How the entity identifies and assesses risks affecting the system","How the entity selects, develops, and performs monitoring activities","How the entity restricts access, manages credentials, and removes rights"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the AICPA Trust Services Criteria (2017), CC6 addresses how the entity restricts logical and physical access, manages user credentials, prevents unauthorized access, and removes access rights when no longer appropriate. It encompasses provisioning, authentication, and access reviews.
Wrong (A): Internal communication about control responsibilities falls under CC2 (Communication and Information), not CC6.
Wrong (B): Identifying and assessing risks is addressed by CC3 (Risk Assessment), not CC6.
Wrong (C): Selecting and developing monitoring activities is addressed by CC4 (Monitoring Activities), not CC6.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3781;

-- Q3785: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Controls the service organization implements as backup measures","Controls tested by the service auditor at the user entity''s site","Controls the subservice organization must implement under contract","Controls user entities must implement to achieve control objectives"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320.A33), complementary user entity controls (CUECs) are controls that the service organization assumes are in place at user entities. These controls complement the service organization''s own controls and are necessary for overall criteria achievement.
Wrong (A): Backup measures implemented by the service organization are the organization''s own controls, not CUECs.
Wrong (B): The service auditor does not test controls at user entity locations as part of a SOC engagement.
Wrong (C): Controls required of subservice organizations are complementary subservice organization controls (CSOCs), not CUECs.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3785;

