-- Q3793: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Encrypt all internal communications using end-to-end encryption protocols","Obtain and communicate relevant quality information to support internal control","Publish all system information on its publicly accessible website","Restrict all communications to formal written channels exclusively"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per the AICPA Trust Services Criteria CC2 (Communication and Information), an entity must obtain and generate relevant, quality information and communicate it internally and externally to support effective internal control functioning. This includes communicating control responsibilities and reporting issues.
Wrong (A): While encryption may be a security control, CC2 addresses the flow and quality of information, not encryption requirements.
Wrong (C): Publishing all system information publicly would violate confidentiality; CC2 requires appropriate communication, not public disclosure.
Wrong (D): CC2 does not restrict communication channels to written-only formats; it requires effective communication through appropriate channels.$EXPL$
