-- Q3794: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Identify and assess risks to objectives, including fraud risks","Quantify all identified risks in precise monetary terms","Eliminate all identified risks before the SOC report is issued","Delegate risk assessment entirely to qualified external consultants"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per the AICPA Trust Services Criteria CC3, an entity must specify clear objectives, identify and analyze risks to achieving those objectives—including fraud risks—and assess potential significant environmental changes affecting internal control. Risk assessment is an ongoing process.
Wrong (B): CC3 requires risk identification and analysis but does not mandate quantifying all risks in monetary terms.
Wrong (C): Eliminating all risks is neither feasible nor required; the entity must assess and manage risks to acceptable levels.
Wrong (D): Management cannot delegate its fundamental responsibility for risk assessment entirely to external parties.$EXPL$
