-- Q3804: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Omit the exceptions from the report since they are isolated incidents","Describe exceptions in the tests and results section for evaluation","Issue an adverse opinion automatically due to any identified exceptions","Communicate the exceptions verbally to management without documentation"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320), all exceptions identified during testing must be described in the tests and results section regardless of whether they are isolated or systemic. The service auditor evaluates the nature, cause, frequency, and significance of exceptions to determine their impact on the opinion.
Wrong (A): Omitting exceptions from the report would misrepresent control performance; all identified exceptions must be disclosed.
Wrong (C): Isolated exceptions do not automatically result in an adverse opinion; the auditor evaluates their aggregate significance.
Wrong (D): Exceptions must be formally documented in the report, not merely communicated verbally to management.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3804;

-- Q3805: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
