  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per AICPA Trust Services Criteria CC2.3, principal service commitments are declarations made to user entities about how the system will perform and be managed, typically found in service level agreements, contracts, and published policies. System requirements flow from these commitments.
Wrong (A): Financial obligations to lenders are debt-related matters, not principal service commitments under the Trust Services framework.
Wrong (B): Employment contracts define obligations to employees, not the service commitments made to user entities.
Wrong (D): Regulatory commitments are compliance obligations, distinct from the service commitments described in the system description.$EXPL$
